I am writing from the Department of English advising office regarding your phone appointment for [date and time]. To make this appointment effective and efficient please follow these key steps.
To prepare for your advising meeting:

•	Make sure your ASU email address is set up, as all correspondence about your academic matters should be made using your ASU email account.

•	Access and review your Degree Audit Report (DARS) before meeting with your advisor. We will be discussing the requirements required for graduation, it is to your benefit to be able to follow along. (Please see https://provost.asu.edu/dars/help/request for instructions on how to retrieve your DARS and https://provost.asu.edu/dars/help/read for help on how to read your DARS.)  

•	Your advisor will call you at your scheduled appointment time. Keep in mind that Arizona is on Mountain Standard Time (MST) and DOES NOT observe daylight savings time (so is essentially on Pacific Standard Time from March – October and Mountain Standard Time from October to March).   

•	Log onto your MyASU page so you can follow along with the advisor during your appointment. Please have a pen and paper ready because appointments can be note intensive. 

•	Prepare a list of questions. We want to make sure that you are prepared for your next semester and we want to help in any way we can, please ask us questions.

We look forward to working with you.

Regards,

Your English Department Advising Team

Shauna Dranetz, shauna.dranetz@asu.edu
